    "blocks": [
      {
        "children": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "Notes on building a deterministic compiler"
          }
        ],
        "id": "usm3w34gb5z5mjxr",
        "level": 1,
        "type": "heading"
      },
      {
        "children": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "By J. Engineer "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "·"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": " 12 minute read"
          }
        ],
        "id": "sl2adi3uhx6wdewz",
        "type": "paragraph"
      },
      {
        "children": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "Determinism is a property you design in, not one you test in afterwards. This post collects the decisions that mattered most on a recent project."
          }
        ],
        "id": "reyqrjaocb2vdpza",
        "type": "paragraph"
      },
      {
        "children": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "Hash the meaning, not the markup"
          }
        ],
        "id": "va43bn4loszqwsld",
        "level": 2,
        "type": "heading"
      },
      {
        "children": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "The single most useful rule was to derive every identifier from the captured meaning of a node rather than from its position in the source tree. Two inputs that mean the same thing then produce the same output."
          }
        ],
        "id": "ojts2srq2s2dsjcv",
        "type": "paragraph"
      },
      {
        "altText": "A block diagram of the four pipeline stages feeding a hash function",
        "caption": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "Figure 1. Each stage is a pure function; the final hash covers the canonical form of the whole tree."
          }
        ],
        "id": "av6giptgafgtfsgf",
        "image": {
          "alt": "A block diagram of the four pipeline stages feeding a hash function",
          "intrinsicHeight": 420,
          "intrinsicWidth": 900,
          "resolved": false,
          "url": "https://blog.example/img/pipeline.png"
        },
        "type": "figure"
      },
      {
        "children": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "As Figure 1 shows, the hash sits at the end of a chain of pure functions. Nothing in that chain reads a clock or the network."
          }
        ],
        "id": "crfalqrm3ntgzmw6",
        "type": "paragraph"
      },
      {
        "children": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "Normalize early, normalize once"
          }
        ],
        "id": "6372pyqltwposky6",
        "level": 2,
        "type": "heading"
      },
      {
        "children": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "Whitespace, line endings, and Unicode form are all normalized at the boundary. Downstream code can then assume a single representation."
          }
        ],
        "id": "22hinzt3njheenea",
        "type": "paragraph"
      },
      {
        "blocks": [
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "value": "If you find yourself normalizing the same value twice, one of the two call sites is in the wrong place."
              }
            ],
            "id": "mkgr6ztj34mk47cw",
            "type": "paragraph"
          }
        ],
        "callout": null,
        "id": "clxlw6ywq2pdakaa",
        "type": "blockquote"
      },
      {
        "altText": "Bar chart of capture timings across twelve fixtures, all under 400 milliseconds",
        "caption": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "Figure 2. Capture-plus-render timings for the fixture corpus."
          }
        ],
        "id": "ko5xknvucu4lr5at",
        "image": {
          "alt": "Bar chart of capture timings across twelve fixtures, all under 400 milliseconds",
          "intrinsicHeight": null,
          "intrinsicWidth": null,
          "resolved": false,
          "url": "https://cdn.example/img/timings.svg"
        },
        "type": "figure"
      },
      {
        "children": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "What I would do differently"
          }
        ],
        "id": "af4vplhr5e2cwofd",
        "level": 2,
        "type": "heading"
      },
      {
        "id": "qti6aclrbu33b5j7",
        "items": [
          {
            "blocks": [
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "value": "Write the fixture runner before the extractor, not after."
                  }
                ],
                "id": "a4j2xksx72caccxc",
                "type": "paragraph"
              }
            ],
            "checked": null,
            "id": "ipiqlsfw2jjqzkrk",
            "type": "listItem"
          },
          {
            "blocks": [
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "value": "Treat \"unsupported\" as a first-class output, with its own diagnostic."
                  }
                ],
                "id": "oohr2nsdd6hgqpow",
                "type": "paragraph"
              }
            ],
            "checked": null,
            "id": "vk6hlhcpt4xftgal",
            "type": "listItem"
          }
        ],
        "ordered": false,
        "start": null,
